In $RR^3$, vector addition composes position vectors along the parallelogram spanned by $vb(a)$ and $vb(b)$, and $lambda vb(a)$ for $lambda in RR$ lies on the line $O A$ with length $abs(lambda vb(a)) = abs(lambda) abs(vb(a))$. In $RR^n$ both operations act componentwise:
$ vb(a) + vb(b) = vecrow(a_1 + b_1, ..., a_n + b_n), quad lambda vb(a) = vecrow(lambda a_1, ..., lambda a_n). $
The same componentwise definitions make $CC^n$ a vector space over $CC$; restricting scalars to $RR$, it is a real vector space of dimension $2n$.
